DESCRIPTION:National French Dip Day marks a sandwich claimed by two Los Ang
 eles restaurants that both opened in 1908 and have been arguing about it e
 ver since. Philippe the Original dates the invention to 1918 and tells a s
 tory about how it happened\; Cole's calls itself the originator and gives 
 no date at all. Nothing available settles which is right — and the obser
 vance's own November 12 date has no traceable origin either.\n\nhttps://to
